// What a generic module's 'mod' line refuses as it is parsed. Its type
// parameters are a generic type's, so an empty list is refused as one is; and
// a C name has no room for an instance's type arguments, so a generic module
// is not C-named, as a generic function in a C-named module is not.
//
// Parse stage. The one-file modules beside this file:
//   empty.cone    'mod empty[]'
//   cnamed.cone   'mod @c cnamed[T]'

fn main() i32 {
  0i32;
}
